        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1777160083692",
            "name": "Select Ledger"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775940580630"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_LLM_LEDGER_ORCH_LEDGER_SELECTOR",
          "id": "1775940523971",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775940523978_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Ledger Selection Assistant\n\n## Purpose\nSelect exactly one ledger from the provided ledger list based on the current user question, chat history, and additional context.\n\n## Input\n- User question: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- Additional Context: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.additional_context}}\n- Ledger list: {{$context.$nodes.GET_DAS_LEDGERS.$output}}\n- Chat History: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n## Core Rule\n- Always return exactly one selected ledger when a valid match or fallback exists.\n- Never return multiple ledgers.\n- For the current user question, consider path 1 only when the user explicitly includes `ledger` or `ledger set`.\n- When path 1 is active, allow best matching by `ledgerName` or `ledgerId` against the provided ledger list.\n\n## Selection Priority\nUse the following order strictly:\n\n1. Current user question\n   - Only consider this path when the current user question explicitly includes `ledger` or `ledger set`.\n   - If the user specifies a ledger name with that qualifier, select the best matching `ledgerName` from the provided ledger list.\n   - If the user specifies a ledger ID with that qualifier, select the best matching `ledgerId` from the provided ledger list.\n\n2. `user_chosen_ledgers` from chat history\n   - If no valid match is found from the current question, and chat history contains a non-empty `user_chosen_ledgers` that exactly matches a `ledgerName` in the provided ledger list, select it.\n\n3. Additional context\n   - If no valid match is found from the current question or `user_chosen_ledgers`, and `additional_context.ledgerContext` exactly matches a `ledgerName` in the provided ledger list, select it.\n\n4. No match\n   - If none of the above yields a valid match from the provided ledger list, return `selectionType = \"none\"` and `selectedLedger = null`.\n\n## Rules\n- The current user question always overrides chat history and incoming context.\n- Do not merge ledgers.\n- Do not return a list of ledgers.\n- For the current user question, use path 1 only when the user explicitly says `ledger` or `ledger set`.\n- For the current user question, match by best-fit `ledgerName` or best-fit `ledgerId`.\n- For `user_chosen_ledgers` and `additional_context.ledgerContext`, match only by exact `ledgerName`.\n- Do not use `ledgerCategory`, `primary`, or `secondary` to select a ledger.\n- If the current user asks for a different ledger than the one in history or context, replace the default with the current-question selection only when path 1 is active and a valid best match is found in the ledger list.\n- If the current user does not mention any ledger, first try `user_chosen_ledgers`; if that is unavailable or does not exactly match a ledger, then try `additional_context.ledgerContext`.\n\n## Deterministic Tie-Break Rules\nWhen more than one candidate matches, choose exactly one using the following order:\n\n1. Best `ledgerName` or best `ledgerId` match from the current question when the question explicitly includes `ledger` or `ledger set`\n2. Exact ledger-name match from `user_chosen_ledgers`\n3. Exact ledger-name match from `additional_context.ledgerContext`\n\n## Matching Logic\n- For the current user question, first check whether the question explicitly includes `ledger` or `ledger set`.\n- If that qualifier is not present, do not use path 1.\n- If the user specifies a ledger name with that qualifier, best-match it against `ledgerName`.\n- If the user specifies a ledger ID with that qualifier, best-match it against `ledgerId`.\n- For path 1, because the qualifier already makes the ledger-selection intent explicit, use the single best match from the provided ledger list instead of requiring an exact match.\n- If `user_chosen_ledgers` is present, match that value against `ledgerName`.\n- If falling back to `additional_context`, use only `ledgerContext` and match it against `ledgerName`.\n- If nothing matches, return `selectionType = \"none\"` and `selectedLedger = null`.\n\n## Output\nReturn only one minified JSON object:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"selectionType\": \"history_selected_ledger|context_selected_ledger|ledger_name|ledger_id|none\",\n  \"selectedLedger\": {\n    \"ledgerId\": \"<string>\",\n    \"ledgerName\": \"<string>\",\n    \"ledgerCategory\": \"<string>\",\n    \"avName\": \"<string|null>\",\n    \"chartOfAccountsId\": \"<string>\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Output Notes\n- `selectedLedger` must be a single object, not an array.\n- If `selectionType = \"none\"`, return:\n\n```json\n{\"selectionType\":\"none\",\"selectedLedger\":null}\n```\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1: Explicit ledger-name selection\nUser question: `show Travel Expenses for company 3000 for ledger Vision Foods USA`\n\nOutput:\n```json\n{\"selectionType\":\"ledger_name\",\"selectedLedger\":{\"ledgerId\":\"1225\",\"ledgerName\":\"Vision Foods - USA Ledger\",\"ledgerCategory\":\"Primary\",\"avName\":\"ora_erp_core_accountBalances_runtime_x__LedgerBalVfusaaccountingflexfield\",\"chartOfAccountsId\":\"54604\"}}\n```\n\n### Example 2: Explicit ledger-ID selection\nUser question: `show Travel Expenses for company 3000 for ledger 1225`\n\nOutput:\n```json\n{\"selectionType\":\"ledger_id\",\"selectedLedger\":{\"ledgerId\":\"1225\",\"ledgerName\":\"Vision Foods - USA Ledger\",\"ledgerCategory\":\"Primary\",\"avName\":\"ora_erp_core_accountBalances_runtime_x__LedgerBalVfusaaccountingflexfield\",\"chartOfAccountsId\":\"54604\"}}\n```\n\n### Example 3: Current user request overrides chat history\nChat history contains non-empty `user_chosen_ledgers` with `Vision Foods - USA IFRS SecLed`\nUser question: `show balances for ledger Vision Foods USA`\n\nOutput:\n```json\n{\"selectionType\":\"ledger_name\",\"selectedLedger\":{\"ledgerId\":\"1225\",\"ledgerName\":\"Vision Foods - USA Ledger\",\"ledgerCategory\":\"Primary\",\"avName\":\"ora_erp_core_accountBalances_runtime_x__LedgerBalVfusaaccountingflexfield\",\"chartOfAccountsId\":\"54604\"}}\n```\n\n### Example 4: No explicit ledger in question, fall back to chat history\nChat history contains `user_chosen_ledgers = Vision Foods - USA Ledger`\nUser question: `show posted journals`\n\nOutput:\n```json\n{\"selectionType\":\"history_selected_ledger\",\"selectedLedger\":{\"ledgerId\":\"1225\",\"ledgerName\":\"Vision Foods - USA Ledger\",\"ledgerCategory\":\"Primary\",\"avName\":\"ora_erp_core_accountBalances_runtime_x__LedgerBalVfusaaccountingflexfield\",\"chartOfAccountsId\":\"54604\"}}\n```\n\n### Example 5: No explicit ledger in question, no history, fall back to additional context\nAdditional context contains `ledgerContext = Vision Foods - USA Ledger`\nUser question: `show balances for trade activity`\n\nOutput:\n```json\n{\"selectionType\":\"context_selected_ledger\",\"selectedLedger\":{\"ledgerId\":\"1225\",\"ledgerName\":\"Vision Foods - USA Ledger\",\"ledgerCategory\":\"Primary\",\"avName\":\"ora_erp_core_accountBalances_runtime_x__LedgerBalVfusaaccountingflexfield\",\"chartOfAccountsId\":\"54604\"}}\n```\n\n### Example 6: No match\nUser question: `show travel expenses and accounting expenses for Vision Africa Zambia`\n\nOutput:\n```json\n{\"selectionType\":\"none\",\"selectedLedger\":null}\n```"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1777160083692",
            "name": "Filter Different Coa Ledgers",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const inputData = $context.$nodes.FIN_GL_LLM_LEDGER_ORCH_LEDGER_SELECTOR.$output;\n\nconst ledger = inputData.selectedLedger || null;\nconst isRecordObject = (value) => value && typeof value === \"object\" && !Array.isArray(value);\nconst normalizeId = (value) => String(value ?? \"\").trim();\nconst resetHierarchyOverrides = (state) => {\n  const currentState = isRecordObject(state) ? { ...state } : {};\n  const shared = isRecordObject(currentState.shared) ? { ...currentState.shared } : {};\n  const hierarchy = isRecordObject(shared.hierarchy) ? { ...shared.hierarchy } : {};\n  hierarchy.hierarchyOverrides = [];\n  shared.hierarchy = hierarchy;\n  return {\n    ...currentState,\n    shared\n  };\n};\nlet res = ledger || null;\n\nif (isRecordObject(ledger)) {\n  const existingAdditionalContext = $context.$variables.additionalContext;\n  const additionalContext = isRecordObject(existingAdditionalContext) ? { ...existingAdditionalContext } : {};\n  const existingChartOfAccountsId = normalizeId(additionalContext.chartOfAccountsId);\n  const ledgerChartOfAccountsId = normalizeId(ledger.chartOfAccountsId);\n  const hasDifferentChartOfAccounts =\n    existingChartOfAccountsId !== \"\" &&\n    ledgerChartOfAccountsId !== \"\" &&\n    existingChartOfAccountsId !== ledgerChartOfAccountsId;\n\n  additionalContext.ledgerId = ledger.ledgerId;\n  additionalContext.ledgerContext = ledger.ledgerName;\n  additionalContext.ledgerCategory = ledger.ledgerCategory;\n  additionalContext.chartOfAccountsId = ledger.chartOfAccountsId;\n  additionalContext.analyticView = ledger.avName;\n\n  res = {\n    ledgerOverride: {\n      ...ledger\n    },\n    additionalContext\n  };\n\n  if (hasDifferentChartOfAccounts) {\n    res.state = resetHierarchyOverrides($context.$variables.state);\n  }\n}\n\nreturn res;\n"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1780483300430"
          },
          "code": "FILTER_DIFFERENT_COA_LEDGERS",
          "id": "1775940580630",
          "inputs": [],
