        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1777160083692",
            "name": "Prepare Presentation Input",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const displayColumnState = $context.$variables.state?.domains?.[`${$context.$variables.routingDecision}_displayColumns`];\n\nconst getPromptSafeTables = (tables) =>\n    Array.isArray(tables)\n        ? tables.map((table) => ({\n            rowLevel: table?.rowLevel,\n            available: table?.available,\n            displayed: table?.displayed,\n            rowsToExclude: table?.rowsToExclude\n        }))\n        : tables;\n\nconst result = {\n    available: displayColumnState?.available,\n    displayed: displayColumnState?.displayed,\n    tables: getPromptSafeTables(displayColumnState?.tables)\n};\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778361009017"
          },
          "code": "PREPARE_PRESENTATION_INPUT",
          "id": "1778361246550",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1777160083692",
            "name": "Presentation Intent Classifier"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778364386256"
          },
          "code": "PRESENTATION_INTENT_CLASSIFIER",
          "id": "1778361009017",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778361009022_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Presentation Intent Classifier\n\n## Objective\n- Classify whether the current user question is a presentation-only request that can be handled by the existing table display workflow.\n- Return only the allowed boolean classification keys in the final JSON object.\n\n## Core Rule\nSet `shouldUsePresentationWorkflow=true` only when all of these are true:\n- The user asks for a local display-only change to the current results/table, such as showing or hiding table columns/attributes, showing all available columns/attributes, showing all currently available rows, rendering the current results as a table, or showing headline/summary/rollup rows as part of the table.\n- There is an existing table display state: `ALL_AVAILABLE_COLUMNS`, `CURRENTLY_SHOWN_COLUMNS`, or `TABLE_DISPLAY_STATE` is present and non-empty.\n- For column/attribute-specific requests, all explicitly requested columns/attributes must be matched to columns in `ALL_AVAILABLE_COLUMNS`, `CURRENTLY_SHOWN_COLUMNS`, or any table entry in `TABLE_DISPLAY_STATE`. If any explicitly requested column/attribute cannot be matched, set shouldUsePresentationWorkflow=false. This does not apply when the user explicitly asks to show all columns/attributes.\n- The request does not change the data that must be retrieved.\n\nOtherwise set `shouldUsePresentationWorkflow=false`.\n\nTreat `shouldUsePresentationWorkflow=true` as \"handle this locally as a presentation-only display change\", including column show/hide requests, show-all-rows requests over the current result, table-rendering requests over the current result, and requests to include headline/summary/rollup rows in the current table.\n\n## Non-Local Presentation Requests\nSet `shouldUsePresentationWorkflow=false` when the user asks to export, download, save, open, send, or convert the results/table/report to another format or tool. These are not local display-only requests.\n\nExport and file-output requests are always `false`, including:\n- `export to Excel`\n- `export to excel`\n- `export to Smart View`\n- `export to smartview`\n- `open in Smart View`\n- `download as CSV`\n- `download the table`\n- `save this as spreadsheet`\n- `send me an Excel file`\n- `convert this to XLSX`\n- `generate a spreadsheet`\n\n## Column Matching Rules\n- Treat `attribute` and `attributes` as synonyms for display/table columns only for presentation-only requests over the current table state.\n- Treat `ALL_AVAILABLE_COLUMNS` as the closed list of columns that may be shown or hidden.\n- Treat `CURRENTLY_SHOWN_COLUMNS` as the closed list of columns already visible.\n- `TABLE_DISPLAY_STATE` may contain row-level table entries with `rowLevel`, `available`, `displayed`, and `rowsToExclude`.\n- When `TABLE_DISPLAY_STATE` is present, treat each table entry's `available` and `displayed` arrays as additional closed lists for matching presentation-only column requests.\n- A requested column is valid when it matches any table entry's `available` or `displayed` column.\n- If the user names a row level using terms such as headline, summary, rollup, total, current-level, child, detail, or detail rows, match only table entries for that row level.\n- If the user does not name a row level and a requested column matches one or more table entries unambiguously as the same business concept, return `true`.\n- Match column names case-insensitively.\n- Ignore spaces, underscores, hyphens, and punctuation when comparing column names.\n- Column names may be technical runtime identifiers. Match the user's requested business label to a similar available column even when the full identifier has prefixes, suffixes, camelCase, snake_case, abbreviations, or domain words around it.\n- A match is valid when the requested label is clearly the same business concept as an available column after normalization, tokenization, or obvious singular/plural handling.\n- Valid similarity examples:\n  - `product` can match `product`, `Product`, `vFProduct`, `productSegment`, `segmentProduct`, `dim_product`, `productName`, or `balancingProduct`\n  - `location` can match `location`, `Location`, `ledgerLocation`, `locationCode`, or `locationSegment`\n  - `division` can match `division`, `Division`, `divisionSegment`, or `reportingDivision`\n  - `intercompany` can match `intercompany`, `interCompany`, `intercompanySegment`, or `icIntercompany`\n- Do not require exact full-string matches.\n- Do not use broad fuzzy guessing. If multiple available columns are plausible and the request does not clearly identify one business concept, return `false`.\n- Allow obvious natural-language variants when the match is unambiguous:\n  - `cost center` can match `costCenter`, `cost_center`, or `Cost Center`\n  - `natural account` can match `naturalAccount`\n  - `account segment` can match `accountSegment`\n  - `ledger currency` can match `ledgerCurrency`\n  - `entered amount` can match `enteredAmount`\n  - `accounted amount` can match `accountedAmount`\n- Do not invent columns. If the requested column is not in `ALL_AVAILABLE_COLUMNS` or `CURRENTLY_SHOWN_COLUMNS`, return `false`.\n- If the user asks to show a column that is already in `CURRENTLY_SHOWN_COLUMNS`, return `true` when the request is otherwise presentation-only. This should be treated as a no-op by downstream display logic.\n- If the user asks to hide a column that is not in `CURRENTLY_SHOWN_COLUMNS` but is in `ALL_AVAILABLE_COLUMNS`, return `true` when the request is otherwise presentation-only. This should be treated as a no-op by downstream display logic.\n- For hide/remove/exclude wording, return `true` only when the user is asking to remove a column from display. Return `false` when the user is asking to remove rows, balances, accounts, companies, cost centers, or other member values from the data.\n- If the user asks generally for `more columns`, `everything`, or `details` without naming a specific available column, return `false`.\n- If the user explicitly asks to `show all columns`, `show me all columns`, `show me all available columns`, `show available attributes`, `show all attributes`, or `show me all available attributes`, return `true` when the request is otherwise presentation-only.\n\n## Remaining Column Listing\nSet `listRemainingColumns=true` only when the user asks to list, identify, or tell them which available, current, remaining, other, hidden, or not-shown columns or attributes can be shown from the current table state, without asking to render those columns in the table.\n\nThis is a presentation-only request when current display state exists because it only describes current table-display metadata.\n\nSet `listRemainingColumns=false` when the user asks to show, add, include, display, or render columns in the table.\n\nSet `shouldUsePresentationWorkflow=false` when `attribute` or `attributes` refers to business/entity metadata rather than current result table columns.\n\n## Row and Table Display Rules\n- Return `true` when the user asks to show all rows, display all rows, show the full table, expand the table, or show the complete current table, and the request is otherwise presentation-only.\n- Return `true` when the user asks to show the current result as a table, show the table, render it as a table, use table view, or switch back to table view, and the request is otherwise presentation-only.\n- Return `true` when the user asks to show the headline, summary, total, subtotal, rollup, or current-level row as part of the table, in the table, or along with table rows, and the request is otherwise presentation-only.\n- Treat row and table display requests as applying only to rows already available in the current result. Do not treat them as requests to retrieve more rows from an agent or backend.\n- Return `false` when `all rows` means a new data retrieval scope, such as all journals, all accounts, all suppliers, all transactions, or all balances.\n- Return `false` when the user asks to filter, remove, hide, exclude, sort, rank, or limit rows by values or conditions.\n\n## Presentation-Only Requests\nThese can be `true` when they satisfy the Core Rule:\n- `show cost center`\n- `show the cost center column`\n- `add natural account`\n- `include available attributes`\n- `include ledger currency`\n- `display entered amount`\n- `put company back`\n- `bring in the intercompany field`\n- `show all columns`\n- `show me all available columns`\n- `show available attributes`\n- `show me all available attributes`\n- `show all attributes`\n- `show all rows`\n- `display all rows`\n- `show the full table`\n- `show this as a table`\n- `switch back to table view`\n- `show headline as part of the table`\n- `include the summary in the table`\n- `show the rollup row in the table`\n- `show total row with the table rows`\n- `show product` when an available column clearly represents product, such as `product`, `productSegment`, or `dim_product`\n- `show location` when an available column clearly represents location, such as `location`, `ledgerLocation`, or `locationCode`\n- `hide cost center`\n- `hide the cost center column`\n- `remove natural account`\n- `exclude ledger currency column`\n- `do not show entered amount`\n- `stop showing product` when a known column clearly represents product\n- `what other columns are available?`\n- `what attributes can I show?`\n- `list remaining columns`\n- `which columns are not shown?`\n- `show me the available attributes` when phrased as a metadata/list question over current results\n\nFor these examples, return `shouldUsePresentationWorkflow=true` and `listRemainingColumns=true`:\n- `what other columns are available?`\n- `what attributes can I show?`\n- `list remaining columns`\n- `which columns are not shown?`\n- `show me the available attributes`\n\nFor these examples, return `shouldUsePresentationWorkflow=true` and `listRemainingColumns=false`:\n- `show all columns`\n- `show all available attributes in the table`\n- `add the remaining columns`\n- `include every available column`\n- `display the other attributes`\n\n## Data-Changing Requests\nSet `shouldUsePresentationWorkflow=false` when the user request changes filters, scope, grouping, aggregation, sorting, time period, ledger, account selection, member values, drilldown, comparison, or data retrieval.\n\nFalse data-changing patterns include:\n- Filter/scope phrases: `for`, `where`, `only`, `in`, `with`, `equals`, `=`, `is`, `greater than`, `less than`\n- Grouping/analysis phrases: `breakdown`, `break down`, `group by`, `split by`, `summarize by`, `total by`, `subtotal by`, `compare by`, `drill down by`, `side by side`\n- Ordering phrases: `sort by`, `order by`, `highest`, `lowest`, `top`, `bottom`\n- Period or ledger changes: `for Jan-25`, `this quarter`, `last month`, `ledger Vision Operations`, `primary ledger`\n- Specific member values, names, or codes used as filters: `cost center 100`, `company 01`, `account 5000`\n- Entity metadata or business-attribute requests where `attribute` does not mean display/table columns, such as `show account 50100's attributes` or `show journal attributes for May`\n\nExamples false:\n- `show balances for cost center 100`\n- `show company 01`\n- `show account 50100's attributes`\n- `show journal attributes for May`\n- `what attributes are available for suppliers?`\n- `only company 01`\n- `where account is 5000`\n- `breakdown by cost center`\n- `group by account segment`\n- `total by company`\n- `compare by cost center`\n- `drill down by account`\n- `sort by entered amount`\n- `show cost center for company 01`\n- `hide rows with zero balance`\n- `exclude company 01`\n- `remove account 5000`\n- `do not show balances for cost center 100`\n- `show all journal rows for May`\n- `show me a table of balances for ledger Vision Operations`\n- `show all accounts`\n- `show all transactions`\n- `export to Excel`\n- `export to Smart View`\n- `open in Smart View`\n- `download as CSV`\n- `save this as spreadsheet`\n- `generate a spreadsheet`\n- `show more columns`\n- `show project` when no project-like column exists in `ALL_AVAILABLE_COLUMNS` or `CURRENTLY_SHOWN_COLUMNS`\n\n## Mixed Requests\n- If the user asks to show/hide a column and also asks to export/download/save/open/convert the results, return `false`.\n- If the user asks both to show/hide a column and to change the data query, return `false`.\n- If any part of the request would require getting a different set of data from an agent or backend query, return `false`.\n- Prefer `false` when the request is ambiguous between showing a column and filtering/grouping by that field.\n\n## Inputs\n\n**Current User Message:** <USER_QUERY>{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}</USER_QUERY>\n\n**All Available Columns:** <ALL_AVAILABLE_COLUMNS>{{JSON.stringify($context.$nodes.PREPARE_PRESENTATION_INPUT.$output.result.available)}}</ALL_AVAILABLE_COLUMNS>\n\n**Currently Shown Columns:** <CURRENTLY_SHOWN_COLUMNS>{{JSON.stringify($context.$nodes.PREPARE_PRESENTATION_INPUT.$output.result.displayed)}}</CURRENTLY_SHOWN_COLUMNS>\n\n**Table Display State:** <TABLE_DISPLAY_STATE>{{JSON.stringify($context.$nodes.PREPARE_PRESENTATION_INPUT.$output.result.tables)}}</TABLE_DISPLAY_STATE>\n\n## Final Output Contract\n\nReturn exactly one minified JSON object.\n\nAllowed keys, exactly:\n- `shouldUsePresentationWorkflow`\n- `listRemainingColumns`\n\nAlways return `listRemainingColumns` as a boolean.\nReturn `listRemainingColumns=false` whenever `shouldUsePresentationWorkflow=false`.\n\nDo not output requested columns, available columns, shown columns, filters, dates, reasoning, markdown, explanations, or any extra keys.\nDo not return markdown or fenced code.\n\nOutput examples:\nFor a presentation-only table display classification:\n```json\n{\"shouldUsePresentationWorkflow\":true,\"listRemainingColumns\":false}\n```\n\nFor a remaining-column listing classification:\n```json\n{\"shouldUsePresentationWorkflow\":true,\"listRemainingColumns\":true}\n```\n\nFor a false classification:\n```json\n{\"shouldUsePresentationWorkflow\":false,\"listRemainingColumns\":false}\n```"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"shouldUsePresentationWorkflow\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"listRemainingColumns\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"shouldUsePresentationWorkflow\",\n    \"listRemainingColumns\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1777160083692",
            "name": "Process Presentation LLM",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const shouldUsePresentationWorkflow =\n    $context.$nodes.PRESENTATION_INTENT_CLASSIFIER.$output.shouldUsePresentationWorkflow;\nconst listRemainingColumns =\n    $context.$nodes.PRESENTATION_INTENT_CLASSIFIER.$output.listRemainingColumns === true;\nconst presentationInput = $context.$nodes.PREPARE_PRESENTATION_INPUT.$output.result || {};\nconst domainState = $context.$variables.state?.domains?.[$context.$variables.routingDecision] || {};\nconst lastUsedData = domainState.lastUsedData || {};\nconst queryResponse = domainState.lastUsedQuery?.queryResponse;\nconst chartOfAccountsSegments =\n    lastUsedData.dataResponse?.avExtractResult?.metadata?.chartOfAccounts?.segments ||\n    queryResponse?.metadata?.chartOfAccounts?.segments ||\n    {};\n\nconst escapeHtml = (value) => String(value ?? \"\")\n    .replaceAll(\"&\", \"&amp;\")\n    .replaceAll(\"<\", \"&lt;\")\n    .replaceAll(\">\", \"&gt;\")\n    .replaceAll('\"', \"&quot;\")\n    .replaceAll(\"'\", \"&#39;\");\n\nconst titleCase = (value) => String(value ?? \"\")\n    .replace(/([a-z0-9])([A-Z])/g, \"$1 $2\")\n    .replace(/[_\\s]+/g, \" \")\n    .trim()\n    .split(\" \")\n    .filter(Boolean)\n    .map((word) => word.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + word.slice(1))\n    .join(\" \");\n\nconst getSegmentLabel = (column) => {\n    const directLabel = chartOfAccountsSegments?.[column]?.label;\n    if (typeof directLabel === \"string\" && directLabel.trim()) {\n        return directLabel;\n    }\n\n    const matchedSegment = Object.values(chartOfAccountsSegments || {})\n        .find((segment) => segment?.dimensionName === column);\n    const matchedLabel = matchedSegment?.label;\n\n    return typeof matchedLabel === \"string\" && matchedLabel.trim() ? matchedLabel : \"\";\n};\n\nconst normalizeColumnName = (column) => {\n    const trimmedColumn = String(column ?? \"\").trim();\n    const segmentLabel = getSegmentLabel(trimmedColumn);\n\n    if (segmentLabel) {\n        return segmentLabel;\n    }\n\n    if (trimmedColumn.endsWith(\"Description\")) {\n        const baseColumn = trimmedColumn.slice(0, -\"Description\".length);\n        const baseLabel = getSegmentLabel(baseColumn);\n\n        return baseLabel ? `${baseLabel} Description` : titleCase(trimmedColumn);\n    }\n\n    if (trimmedColumn.endsWith(\"TreeFilter\")) {\n        const baseColumn = trimmedColumn.slice(0, -\"TreeFilter\".length);\n        const baseLabel = getSegmentLabel(baseColumn);\n\n        return baseLabel ? `${baseLabel} Tree Filter` : titleCase(trimmedColumn);\n    }\n\n    return titleCase(trimmedColumn);\n};\n\nconst appendRemainingColumns = (remainingColumns, available, displayed) => {\n    const displayedColumns = new Set(Array.isArray(displayed) ? displayed : []);\n\n    for (const column of Array.isArray(available) ? available : []) {\n        if (!displayedColumns.has(column) && !remainingColumns.includes(column)) {\n            remainingColumns.push(column);\n        }\n    }\n};\n\nconst getRemainingColumns = () => {\n    const remainingColumns = [];\n    const tables = Array.isArray(presentationInput.tables) ? presentationInput.tables : [];\n\n    if (tables.length > 0) {\n        for (const table of tables) {\n            appendRemainingColumns(remainingColumns, table?.available, table?.displayed);\n        }\n\n        return remainingColumns;\n    }\n\n    appendRemainingColumns(remainingColumns, presentationInput.available, presentationInput.displayed);\n    return remainingColumns;\n};\n\nconst buildRemainingColumnsResponse = () => {\n    const remainingColumns = getRemainingColumns();\n    const data = remainingColumns.length === 0\n        ? \"<p>All available columns are already shown.</p>\"\n        : `<p>Remaining available columns:</p><ul>${remainingColumns.map((column) => `<li>${escapeHtml(normalizeColumnName(column))}</li>`).join(\"\")}</ul>`;\n\n    return [{\n        display_type: \"text\",\n        data\n    }];\n};\n\nconst result = {\n    routingSwitchPath : shouldUsePresentationWorkflow ? \"ora_fin_gl_ledger_agent_orchestrator\" : $context.$variables.routingDecision,\n};\nif (shouldUsePresentationWorkflow && listRemainingColumns) {\n    result.orchestratorObj = {\n        listRemainingColumns: true,\n        agentResponse: buildRemainingColumnsResponse()\n    };\n} else if(shouldUsePresentationWorkflow){\n    result.orchestratorObj = {\n        path: \"presentation\"\n    }\n}\n\nreturn result;"
          },
