        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1777160083692",
            "name": "Summarization Fallback"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1777162655343"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARIZATION_FALLBACK",
          "id": "1777162614546",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777162614551_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Objective\n\nConvert an input JSON array into one JSON object that matches the output schema exactly.\n\n## Limitations\n\n- Do not include any additional narration or context.\n- Do not create your own Follow-up Actions.\n- Under **NO** circumstance will <a href=\"\" \"target=\"_blank\">here</a> **EVER** be printed.\n\n## Input\n\nA single JSON array of 1+ objects.\n\ninput: {{$context.$nodes.SUMMARIZATION_PRE_PROCESSOR.$output.result.agentOutput}}\n\ncurrent agent: {{$context.$nodes.SUMMARIZATION_PRE_PROCESSOR.$output.result.agentName}}\n\n## Return Contract\n\nSchema (single minified JSON object):\n{ \"agent\": <current agent string>, \"intent\":<string>, \"schema_version\":\"1\", \"title\":<string>, \"description\":<string>,\"user_chosen_ledgers\": <string>, \"selectedHierarchies\":<string>,\"timestamp\":\"dd-mm-yyyy HH:MM\", \"topicName\":<string>, \"category\":<string>, \"agent_response\": [<blocks>] }\n\n- keep title and description very short and concise\n- category string value will be one of the following based on current agent:\n  - ora_fin_gl_journals_assistant → \"journal\"\n  - ora_fin_gl_balance_inquiry_and_analysis_assistant → \"balances\"\n  - ora_fin_gl_financial_reporting_assistant → \"report\"\n  - ora_fin_gl_subledger_supporting_details_assistant → \"subledgerJournals\"\n  - ora_fin_gl_general_ledger_functions_assistant → \"glf\"\n  - ora_fin_gl_help_topic_assistant → \"help\"\n  - ora_fin_gl_process_exceptions_assistant → \"exceptions\"\n  - ora_fin_fun_insights_assistant → \"insights\"\n  - ora_fin_gl_export_to_excel_assistant → \"exportexcel\"\n  - ora_fin_gl_hierarchy_manager_assistant → \"hierarchy\"\n\nFor each input item in order:\n1. If item contains attribute \"type\": \"metadata\"\n   - Do not build a block for this item\n   - Take \"toolTimeStamp\" as value for schema timestamp\n   - Take \"intent\" as value for schema intent\n2. Else, determine block type using item.display_type\n   - Build block\n     - Text: text = item.data\n       - Do not merge with other text blocks\n       - Do not strip HTML\n     - List: strip all HTML, produce fields.items as simple text lines\n     - Table: strip HTML; pass through values.\n     - Action: set actions.items as item.data\n   - display_sequence starts at 1 and increments by 1.\n\n## Block Definitions\n\n- Each block will be a single minified JSON object\n- Within each block, emit keys in the exact order shown and do not emit any new key until the current nested value (object or array) is fully closed.\n- Begin with building the outer schema first.\n  - For schemas with arrays, create empty arrays first.\n  - Build each array item (rowItems,columnItems,fieldItems) one by one, ensuring each object is properly formed and closed json before creating the next one\n\n### Text\n\nSchema: { \"display_type\":\"text\", \"display_sequence\":<n>, \"text\":\"<string>\" }\n- Text properties exact order: display_type, display_sequence, text\n\n### Table\n\nSchema: { \"display_type\":\"table\", \"display_sequence\":<n>, \"rows\":{\"items\":[<rowItems>]}, \"columns\":{\"items\":[<columnItems>]}, \"keyAttributes\":{\"items\":[\"<primary field>\"]}, \"accessibility\":{\"aria-label\":\"<summary>\",\"row.accessible-row-header\":\"<primary field>\"} }\n- Table properties exact order: display_type, display_sequence, rows, columns, keyAttributes, accessibility\n\nrowItem: json object\n```json\n{ \"<column>\": \"<value>\" }\n```\n\ncolumnItem: json object; properties exact order → headerText, field, id, resizable, className, template\n\n{ \"headerText\":\"<label>\",\"field\":\"<column>\",\"id\":\"<column>\",\"resizable\":\"enabled\",\"className\":\"\",\"template\":\"monetaryTemplate|dateTemplate|deepLinkTemplate\"}\n\n### List\n\nSchema: {\"display_type\":\"list\",\"display_sequence\":<n>,\"header\":\"<string>\",\"fields\":{\"items\":[ {\"id\":\"<string>\",\"value\":\"<string>\"} ] },\"keyAttributes\":{\"items\":[\"<id1>\", \"...\"]},\"accessibility\":{\"aria-label\":\"<string>\"},\"selection_mode\":\"none\"}\n\n- Property order: display_type, display_sequence, header, fields, keyAttributes, accessibility, selection_mode\n- fields.items id generation: id = \"item-\" + (1-based index per list block). Do not reuse across blocks.\n- keyAttributes.items must contain the ids of all fieldItems in the list block, in order.\n\nExample:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"display_type\": \"list\",\n  \"display_sequence\": 1,\n  \"header\": \"Sample Header\",\n  \"fields\": {\n    \"items\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"item-1\",\n        \"value\": \"This is step 1.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"item-2\",\n        \"value\": \"this is step 2.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"keyAttributes\": {\n    \"items\": [\"item-1\", \"item-2\"]\n  },\n  \"accessibility\": {\n    \"aria-label\": \"This is a string.\"\n  },\n  \"selection_mode\": \"none\"\n}\n```\n\nList Self-check (perform silently before returning):\n\n- The last object inside fields.items array ends with }\n- fields/items closure and alignment:\n  - The last non-space character before the closing ] of fields.items must be }.\n  - Brace balance inside fields.items: count(\"{\") == count(\"}\")\n\n### Action\n\nSchema:\n{ \"display_type\":\"action\", \"display_sequence\":<n>, \"actions\":{\"items\":[\"<question 1>\", \"<question ...>\"]}}\n\n- Action properties exact order: display_type, display_sequence, actions\n\n### Common Formatting Rules\n\n- No HTML in list or table blocks. Text blocks may use <b> for amounts.\n- Table columns: columns[].className=\"\"; set template only when item specifies monetary/date/deeplink.\n- Always emit the following curly-brace templates as a single JSON string value (the entire template in double quotes). Inside the template, do not use any quotes at all:\n  - Amounts: {amount:<number>,currency:<ISO_code>}\n  - Dates (ISO): {date:<YYYY-MM-DD>}\n  - Percentages: <decimal>%\n  - Relative|External links: leave templates exactly as received as a single string value (do not modify text inside curly braces)\n- Maintain stable key order; output must be valid JSON (no markdown, no trailing commas, no escaped newlines).\n- Json closure discipline:\n  - Never start emitting the next sibling key until the current object/array is fully closed.\n- html Anchor elements <a></a> strictly prohibited.\n\n## Error handling\n\n- If input is missing/incomplete or cannot be parsed/transformed, return the schema with agent_response containing exactly one text block with short direct message: \"We couldn’t complete your request right now. Please try again later.\"\n\n## Self-check (perform silently before returning):\n\n- display_sequence starts at 1 with no gaps\n- Only supported display types used\n- All currency/dates/percentages/links use curly braces\n- Return contract is valid JSON; minified; no trailing commas; no narration\n- Re-parse your output mentally as JSON; if parsing would fail, regenerate once more. If regeneration fails again, go to error handling."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
