          "code": "LLM_FLAGS",
          "id": "1778144630697",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778144630698_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Ledger Agent Metadata Flags\n\n## Objective\n- Classify boolean metadata fields for Oracle Fusion Cloud ERP ledger-related requests.\n- Return only the three boolean flags in the final JSON object.\n\n## Inputs\n\n**Current User Message:** <USER_QUERY>{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}</USER_QUERY>\n\n**Additional Context:** <ADDITIONAL_CONTEXT>{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.additional_context}}</ADDITIONAL_CONTEXT>\n\n**History Message:** <CHAT_HISTORY> {{$context.$variables.compactedChatHistory}} </CHAT_HISTORY>\n\n## Flags To Classify\n- `hasExplicitLedgerReference`\n- `hasHierarchyRelatedIntent`\n- `potentialPresentationChangeOnly`\n\n## Chat History Usage\n- Classify primarily from the current USER_QUERY.\n- Use chat history only when a flag explicitly allows it.\n- If chat history or additional context contains another JSON schema, ignore that schema completely. Only the final output contract in this prompt is valid.\n\n## Flag Rules\n\n### hasExplicitLedgerReference\nSet `hasExplicitLedgerReference=true` when the current USER_QUERY contains an explicit ledger qualifier: `ledger`, `ledgers`, `ledger set`, `ledger sets`, `ledgerset`, or `ledgersets`, case-insensitive.\n\nExamples true:\n- `show balances for Vision Operations Ledger`\n- `Show total journal activity for ledger set VF_US_Combined`\n\nExamples false:\n- `show balances for cost center 100`\n- `trial balance for May`\n\n### hasHierarchyRelatedIntent\nSet `hasHierarchyRelatedIntent=true` only when one of these conditions is met:\n\n- The USER_QUERY is an explicit request to list, show, or view hierarchies, trees, or tree versions for one or more COA segments.\n- The USER_QUERY is an explicit request to change, switch, set, or use a hierarchy, tree, or tree version for one or more COA segments.\n- The USER_QUERY is an explicit request to show, view, list, or retrieve current, saved, or default hierarchy preferences.\n- The USER_QUERY is an explicit request to clear, remove, reset, or delete a saved/default hierarchy preference for a COA segment.\n- The USER_QUERY is a reply that selects a hierarchy from an active hierarchy-selection or hierarchy-recovery flow in CHAT_HISTORY. CHAT_HISTORY must contain a hierarchy-selection table for a requested segment with hierarchy options. The flow may have started from an explicit hierarchy request, a missing hierarchy for a segment, or a requested COA segment value that is not present in the current hierarchy selection.\n- The USER_QUERY is a reply that requests saving the selected hierarchy as the default, and CHAT_HISTORY contains the hierarchy-confirmation prompt: `I’ll use <treeVersionName> as the <label> hierarchy. Save this as your new default preference?`\n- The USER_QUERY is a reply that requests using the selected hierarchy only for this session, and CHAT_HISTORY contains the hierarchy-confirmation prompt: `I’ll use <treeVersionName> as the <label> hierarchy. Save this as your new default preference?`\n\nSet `hasHierarchyRelatedIntent=false` for plain breakdown, grouping, filtering, display, or presentation requests by company, cost center, account, intercompany, or other COA segments when the current input and relevant history do not explicitly mention hierarchy/tree concepts.\nDo not set `hasHierarchyRelatedIntent=true` merely because the USER_QUERY uses hierarchy-shaped analysis words such as `children`, `child`, `descendants`, `last descendants`, `direct children`, `immediate descendants`, `next level under`, or `one level under`. These are breakdown/drilldown intents unless the user explicitly asks to list, change, save, clear, or choose a hierarchy, tree, tree version, or hierarchy preference.\n\nExamples true:\n- `Show me the active hierarchies for Company.`\n- `List tree versions for the Account segment.`\n- `Show hierarchies where account 5000 exists`\n- `Change division hierarchy.`\n- `Change hierarchy for cost center.`\n- `List my current hierarchy preferences.`\n- `Show my saved hierarchy preferences.`\n- `Clear my default hierarchy for Account.`\n- `Remove the saved hierarchy preference for Company.`\n- `2` when CHAT_HISTORY contains a hierarchy-selection table for a requested segment with hierarchy options.\n- `Use 3.` when CHAT_HISTORY contains a hierarchy-selection table for a requested segment with hierarchy options.\n- `Choose 2nd one` when CHAT_HISTORY contains a hierarchy-selection table for a requested segment with hierarchy options.\n- `Use VF GM and Income-Current.` when CHAT_HISTORY contains a hierarchy-selection table for a requested segment with hierarchy options.\n- `2` when the prior assistant turn showed hierarchy options because no hierarchy was configured for the requested segment.\n- `Use 3.` when the prior assistant turn showed hierarchy options because a requested COA segment value was not present in the current hierarchy selection.\n- `Save as Default.` when CHAT_HISTORY contains the hierarchy-confirmation prompt.\n- `This Session Only.` when CHAT_HISTORY contains the hierarchy-confirmation prompt.\n\nExamples false:\n- `breakdown by cost center`\n- `breakdown by children of account 10000`\n- `breakdown by descendants of account 10000`\n- `drill down to immediate descendants of company 5000`\n- `expand on direct children of company 5000`\n- `breakdown one level under company 5000`\n- `show balance for last descendants of account 10000`\n- `show company 100 by child companies`\n- `show for children of account 56010`\n- `group by company and account`\n- `show cost center`\n- `show cost center column`\n- `show for cost center A`\n- `include account segment`\n\n### potentialPresentationChangeOnly\nClassify `potentialPresentationChangeOnly` from the current USER_QUERY. Do not use this flag to change the values of `hasExplicitLedgerReference` or `hasHierarchyRelatedIntent`.\n\nSet `potentialPresentationChangeOnly=true` only when the current USER_QUERY asks to change display/presentation of existing results without changing the data being retrieved.\n\nTrue presentation-only requests include showing, hiding, adding, including, excluding, or removing:\n- columns\n- fields\n- measures\n- generic COA segment columns\n- all rows already available in the current result\n- the current result as a table/table view\n- display/table attributes when used as column synonyms\n\nTreat generic segment names as presentation-only when they are used as display columns/fields, including:\n- company\n- cost center\n- account\n- account segment\n- natural account\n- balancing segment\n- intercompany\n- department\n\nExamples true:\n- `show cost center`\n- `show cost center column`\n- `add cost center`\n- `include available attributes`\n- `show available attributes`\n- `show all attributes`\n- `show me all available attributes`\n- `include account segment`\n- `remove entered amounts`\n- `hide accounted amount`\n- `don't show company`\n- `exclude intercompany column`\n- `show all rows`\n- `display all rows`\n- `show this as a table`\n- `switch back to table view`\n\nSet `potentialPresentationChangeOnly=false` when the current USER_QUERY changes filters, scope, grouping, aggregation, drilldown, comparison, sorting, time period, ledger, account selection, member values, or data retrieval.\n\nFalse data-changing requests include:\n- filter/scope phrases such as `for`, `where`, `only`, `in`, `with`, `equals`, `=`, `is`, `greater than`, `less than`\n- grouping/analysis phrases such as `breakdown`, `break down`, `group by`, `split by`, `summarize by`, `total by`, `compare by`, `drill down by`, `side by side`\n- specific COA member values, names, or codes used as filters\n- file-output or external-tool phrases such as `export`, `download`, `save`, `open in`, `send`, `convert`, `Excel`, `CSV`, `XLSX`, `spreadsheet`, `Smart View`, or `smartview`\n\nExamples false:\n- `show for cost center A`\n- `show account 50100's attributes`\n- `show journal attributes for May`\n- `show balances for cost center 100`\n- `only company 01`\n- `where account is 5000`\n- `breakdown by cost center`\n- `group by account segment`\n- `total by company`\n- `compare by cost center`\n- `drill down by account`\n- `show all journal rows for May`\n- `show me a table of balances for ledger Vision Operations`\n- `show all accounts`\n- `show all transactions`\n- `export to excel`\n- `export to smartview`\n- `open in Smart View`\n- `download as CSV`\n- `download the table`\n- `save this as spreadsheet`\n- `send me an Excel file`\n- `convert this to XLSX`\n- `generate a spreadsheet`\n- `show balances side by side for May-26 and Jun-26`\n\n## Final Output Contract\n\nReturn exactly one minified JSON object.\n\nAllowed keys, exactly:\n- `hasExplicitLedgerReference`\n- `hasHierarchyRelatedIntent`\n- `potentialPresentationChangeOnly`\n\nDo not output `agent`, `routingReasoning`, `reasons`, `accountingPeriod`, filters, dates, columns, nested objects, markdown, explanations, or any keys from chat history/additional context.\ndo not return markdown or fenced code\n\nRequired shape:\n```json\n{\"hasExplicitLedgerReference\":false,\"hasHierarchyRelatedIntent\":false,\"potentialPresentationChangeOnly\":false}\n```"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"hasExplicitLedgerReference\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"hasHierarchyRelatedIntent\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"potentialPresentationChangeOnly\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"hasExplicitLedgerReference\",\n    \"hasHierarchyRelatedIntent\",\n    \"potentialPresentationChangeOnly\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "Gpt-5 Mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "errorNodeId": "1777160083692",
            "name": "Determine Intent Routing"
          },
          "outcomes": {
